      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Solifluction is specifically associated with periglacial environments where saturated surface soil slides over impermeable permafrost.",
        "Soil creep is frequently tested via its field indicators, such as bent tree trunks, tilted utility poles, and broken retaining walls.",
        "Distinguish between a Slide (movement along a distinct plane of rupture) and a Flow (viscous fluid-like motion of saturated material)."
